{"title":"Career roadmap · Plant Operations Engineer","role":"Plant Operations Engineer","summary":"A Plant Operations Engineer is responsible for keeping an industrial process plant operating safely, efficiently and reliably. The role sits at the intersection of chemical-process engineering, equipment, process control, production, safety, maintenance and operations management.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Graduate Engineer Trainee, Process Engineer, Production Engineer, Operations Engineer"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"What should I specialise in?","output":"Process operations, process control, production, utilities, safety or reliability"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Operations/Process Engineer, Shift Engineer, Operations Lead"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How do I remain relevant?","output":"Plant Operations Manager, Process Engineering Manager, Production Head or Operations Director"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a Chemical Engineering graduate, this is a directly aligned career path."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical industries include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Oil & gas"},{"text":"Petrochemicals"},{"text":"Refineries"},{"text":"Fertilisers"},{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Specialty chemicals"},{"text":"Food processing"},{"text":"Cement and minerals"},{"text":"Polymers"},{"text":"Paints and coatings"},{"text":"Pulp and paper"},{"text":"Water treatment"},{"text":"Energy and utilities"},{"text":"Battery and advanced-materials manufacturing"}]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build this","Key skills","Proof of progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Chemical engineering fundamentals"},{"text":"Mathematics, chemistry, physics, material balances"},{"text":"Process calculation portfolio"}],[{